 "notes": "All four regions NSS serves are current; none is left out. Southard and Veilleux, SIR 2014-5165 (version 1.0): rural regions 1 (Central Lowlands, 131 gages), 2 (Ozark Plateaus, 135) and 3 (Mississippi Alluvial Plain, 12), at 8 AEPs, replacing Alexander and Wilson (1995). Equations, SEP in percent and AVP from Tables 7-9; ranges from Table 14; t, model error variance and the matrix (order intercept, log10 DRNAREA, log10 BSHAPE) from the Table 10 workbook. Southard, SIR 2010-5073: statewide urban set on DRNAREA and IMPNLCD01 from 35 gages at 7 AEPs (the report publishes no 0.5-percent AEP), which the 2014 rural report does not replace, since it covers basins with about 5 percent or less impervious area. Equations from Table 5; the constant is printed, so intercept = log10 of it; ranges from Table 9; model error variance and the matrix (order intercept, log10 DRNAREA, IMPNLCD01) from Table 8. The urban set overlaps the rural regions, and a caller chooses with region=. The citation for 2010-5073 is the report's own suggested citation, whose title (Estimating) differs from its cover (Estimation). Neither report has a worked example. Every coefficient and range equals NSS, and so do the SEPs, the rural ones to 5e-7 and the urban ones within 0.00015, inside Table 7's rounding. The rural equations reproduce all 278 gages of Table 4 at all 8 AEPs from Table 5's rounded inputs, within 0.7 percent, and the urban equations all 35 gages of Table 4 at all 7 AEPs, within 0.6 percent, and all 7 of Table 11. Covariance checks: MEV + xUx reproduces all 2,224 regression variances of the rural Table 12 within 0.001, and of the five other orders the next best misses region 1 by 0.0027; its mean over the gages reproduces Tables 7-9's AVP within 0.001, and the urban mean reproduces Table 7 within 0.001. Printed t: region 3's 1.782 is t(0.95, 12), where n-p is 10 and t is 1.812; flowfreq takes t from n_sites - p, so region 3 intervals use 1.812. Regions 1, 2 and Urban agree with the printed 1.66 and 1.694. SIR 2010-5073 inconsistencies, none in a stored value: Table 7's average errors labelled logarithm units are variances (0.013 is -23.1 to +30.0 percent), stored as avp, and sep_log is their root, as NSS has it; Table 9's mean impervious area of 6.5 is a misprint of 26.5 (Table 2 averages 26.47, and Table 10's sensitivities need 26.5); Table 10's -10 percent drainage-area row (-1.9) should be about -6. Not stored: Table 13's drainage-area-only exponents and constants for the area-ratio method (region 3's equal Table 9), and pseudo-R2 and SEM. Weighted columns do not fully reproduce and are not stored: SIR 2014-5165's WIE differs from equation 5 by more than 0.6 percent at 569 of 2,224 values (up to 9 percent) and prints a gage number as the 10-percent WIE at 05506350; SIR 2010-5073's W values imply a regression variance near 0.0001 where Table 8 gives about 0.01, and two are misprinted (340 at 06893600, 86 at 06910200).",
